    "version": "5.46",
    "title": "Profile customization — bio, custom title, theme, pinned hero & match",
    "published_at": "2026-04-30",
    "content": "Signed-in players can now personalise their profile page. Everything is gated behind the new `profile_customization` preview flag (default `off`) so it stays invisible to the public until a superuser flips it in the Admin Panel.\n\n• New `player_profiles` table (id SERIAL PK, account_id BIGINT UNIQUE) holds the bio (≤300 chars), custom title, theme accent colour, pinned hero (id + optional ≤80-char caption) and pinned match id. One row per player, upsert on save, no migration needed thanks to CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS in initDb().\n• New cosmetic catalogue (`src/profileCosmetics.js` + mirror `web/src/profileCosmetics.js`) defines the FREE titles (\"Inhouse Veteran\", \"First Bloodhound\", etc.), PREMIUM titles (\"Tournament Champion\", \"Hall of Famer\", \"Pro Member\"), FREE accent colours (blue / green / red / amber / purple), and PREMIUM accent colours (gold, neon-pink, cyan). Validators (isValidTitle / isValidTheme / isPremiumTitle / isPremiumTheme) are shared by client and server so the dropdowns never desync from the API.\n• Three new endpoints on the web server: `GET /api/me/profile` returns the signed-in player's customization plus `is_pro`, `POST /api/me/profile` upserts after validating bio length, premium gating (403), pinned-match ownership (the match must be one the player actually played in), and the title/theme catalogue, and `GET /api/player/:id/profile-card` is the public read used by the profile page — it denormalises the pinned match (winner / duration / start time + the player's own row in that match for hero & KDA) so the card renders in one round trip.\n• New settings page at `/settings/profile` (lazy-loaded, mirrors the SettingsNotifications layout). Sections: Basics (textarea bio with live char counter), Custom title (radio list — premium options shown with a 🔒 PRO pill and disabled until Pro tier ships), Theme accent (swatch picker — premium swatches locked the same way), Pinned hero (typeahead over ALL_HEROES with hero icons + optional caption input), Pinned match (dropdown populated from the player's own recent matches via the existing /api/players/:id endpoint). A live preview card at the top updates as you type so you can see exactly what other players will see before saving.\n• PlayerProfile renders the customization: theme accent paints a left border on the title/bio block (no global recolour), the custom title appears in uppercase under the player name, the bio shows in italic muted text, and the pinned hero / pinned match render as compact cards with the same accent border. An \"✏️ Edit Profile\" link sits next to the Share button when you're viewing your own profile (gated on the flag + Steam-linked own-profile check).\n• Premium hooks for Pro tier — server-side `_isProAccount(accountId)` is a stub that returns false today, so any attempt to save a premium title or theme returns 403 even if a client tampered with the dropdown. When the Pro tier ships, replacing the stub is the only change needed; the route shape, validators and catalogue all stay the same.",
    "author": "System"
